Parallel Structure
Rules
- A parallel structure is used when multiple actions occur simultaneously
- A fork node must be used to split the flow into parallel edges
- Each edge represents an independent action that can occur at the same time
- All parallel edges must eventually join back into a single flow using a join node
- Do not use decision nodes for parallel behavior
- Parallel edges should not depend on each other
- After the join node, the process continues as a single sequence

Keywords
Parallel structures are often indicated by:
- "in parallel"
- "simultaneously"
- "at the same time"
- "meanwhile"
- "concurrently"
These keywords indicate that multiple actions should occur at the same time.

The following examples show how parallel structures are represented in JSON model.

