  ]
}

Overall Example
The following example demonstrates how multiple control flow structures (decision, nested decision, and merging) are combined.
Text:
A customer enters an order.
If the order total is more than 10000 euros:
- The manager reviews the order.
- If the order is approved, the inventory manager allocates the stock.
- Otherwise, the order is cancelled.
If the order total is not more than 10000 euros:
- The inventory manager allocates the stock.
After stock allocation:
- If the stock level is too low, the product is reordered.

Output:
{
  "nodes": [
    {"id": "n1", "type": "initial"},
    {"id": "n2", "type": "action", "label": "enter order"},
    {"id": "n3", "type": "decision", "label": "order total > 10000?"},
    {"id": "n4", "type": "action", "label": "review order"},
    {"id": "n5", "type": "decision", "label": "order approved?"},
    {"id": "n6", "type": "action", "label": "cancel order"},
    {"id": "n7", "type": "merge"}, // Used to merge edges with values ​​>10000 (approved) and <=10000.
    {"id": "n8", "type": "action", "label": "allocate stock"}, // The only action node
    {"id": "n9", "type": "decision", "label": "stock level low?"},
    {"id": "n10", "type": "action", "label": "reorder product"},
    {"id": "n11", "type": "merge"},
    {"id": "n12", "type": "final"}
  ],
  "edges": [
    {"source": "n1", "target": "n2"},
    {"source": "n2", "target": "n3"},
    {"source": "n3", "target": "n4", "label": "yes"},
    {"source": "n3", "target": "n7", "label": "no"}, // directly connect to merge
    {"source": "n4", "target": "n5"},
    {"source": "n5", "target": "n7", "label": "yes"}, // Approved applications will be redirected to the merge page.
    {"source": "n5", "target": "n6", "label": "no"},
    {"source": "n6", "target": "n11"}, // Cancelled applications will skip allocate and directly merge to the end.
    {"source": "n7", "target": "n8"},
    {"source": "n8", "target": "n9"},
    {"source": "n9", "target": "n10", "label": "yes"},
    {"source": "n9", "target": "n11", "label": "no"},
    {"source": "n10", "target": "n11"},
    {"source": "n11", "target": "n12"}
  ]
}

Output Format:
Return ONLY a valid JSON model that strictly follows the structure below.
Do not include any explanation, text, or markdown formatting.
{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "string",
      "type": "initial | action | decision | merge | fork | join | final",
      "label": "string (optional)"
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
      "source": "n1",
      "target": "n2",
      "label": "string (optional)"
    }
  ]
}

Rules:
- Node IDs must use the format "n1", "n2", "n3", ...
- Use "label" for action, object, and decision descriptions when helpful
- Use edge "label" for edge labels such as "yes" or "no"
- Do not include any explanation
